1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:16,187
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June seventeenth. The price of chicken in Japan has climbed to its highest level on record — and a weaker yen is a big part of the reason. Let's listen.

2
00:00:16,788 --> 00:00:19,547
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:20,248 --> 00:00:26,032
[News] 鶏肉の値段が、今までで一番高くなりました。

4
00:00:26,731 --> 00:00:35,707
[News] 国の調査によると、鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、157円でした。

5
00:00:36,408 --> 00:00:44,231
[News] これは、2015年に記録をとり始めてから、一番高い値段です。

6
00:00:44,932 --> 00:00:50,164
[News] 値段が上がった理由の一つは、円安です。

7
00:00:50,863 --> 00:00:57,631
[News] 円が安いと、外国から買うニワトリのエサが高くなります。

8
00:00:58,332 --> 00:01:05,676
[News] エサが高くなると、鶏肉を作るお金も増えて、値段が上がります。

9
00:01:06,376 --> 00:01:13,647
[News] 牛肉や、外国から運ばれる肉の値段も、高くなっています。

10
00:01:14,347 --> 00:01:21,715
[News] 毎日の食事を作る家庭にとって、厳しい状況が続いています。

11
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:29,760
[News] お店では、少しでも安い肉を選ぶお客さんが増えているそうです。

12
00:01:30,459 --> 00:01:32,091
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:32,691 --> 00:01:39,292
[Slow] 鶏肉の値段が、今までで一番高くなりました。

14
00:01:40,091 --> 00:01:43,739
[Host] The price of chicken has become the highest it has ever been.

15
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:46,427
[Vocab] 値段

16
00:01:46,828 --> 00:01:54,507
[Host] It means price — how much something costs. A very everyday word; you'll see it on every shelf and menu.

17
00:01:55,108 --> 00:02:05,379
[Slow] 国の調査によると、鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、157円でした。

18
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:13,907
[Host] According to a national survey, the average price of one hundred grams of chicken was one hundred fifty-seven yen.

19
00:02:14,508 --> 00:02:16,692
[Vocab] 調査

20
00:02:17,092 --> 00:02:25,348
[Host] It means a survey or investigation — looking into something carefully. The government does one to track prices across the whole country.

21
00:02:25,948 --> 00:02:34,900
[Slow] これは、2015年に記録をとり始めてから、一番高い値段です。

22
00:02:35,699 --> 00:02:40,644
[Host] This is the highest price since they began keeping records in twenty fifteen.

23
00:02:41,243 --> 00:02:43,475
[Vocab] 記録

24
00:02:43,876 --> 00:02:51,580
[Host] It means a record — written-down data, or a best-ever mark in sports. Here it's the kept data on prices over the years.

25
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:58,156
[Slow] 値段が上がった理由の一つは、円安です。

26
00:02:58,955 --> 00:03:01,764
[Host] One reason the price went up is the weak yen.

27
00:03:02,364 --> 00:03:04,812
[Vocab] 円安

28
00:03:05,211 --> 00:03:16,324
[Host] It means a weak yen — when the yen is worth less against other money. The first character is yen, the second means cheap. A cheap yen makes imports expensive.

29
00:03:16,924 --> 00:03:24,651
[Slow] 円が安いと、外国から買うニワトリのエサが高くなります。

30
00:03:25,451 --> 00:03:30,611
[Host] When the yen is cheap, the chicken feed bought from abroad becomes more expensive.

31
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:33,228
[Vocab] エサ

32
00:03:33,627 --> 00:03:41,764
[Host] It means feed or food for animals. Much of Japan's chicken feed is imported, so its cost rides on the exchange rate.

33
00:03:42,364 --> 00:03:50,668
[Slow] 牛肉や、外国から運ばれる肉の値段も、高くなっています。

34
00:03:51,467 --> 00:03:56,484
[Host] Beef, and meat brought in from abroad, are also getting more expensive.

35
00:03:57,084 --> 00:03:59,508
[Vocab] 牛肉

36
00:03:59,907 --> 00:04:08,163
[Host] It means beef. The first character is cow, the second is meat. The same pattern gives you chicken meat and pork.

37
00:04:08,764 --> 00:04:17,187
[Slow] 毎日の食事を作る家庭にとって、厳しい状況が続いています。

38
00:04:17,987 --> 00:04:23,052
[Host] For households that cook every day, a tough situation continues.

39
00:04:23,651 --> 00:04:26,052
[Vocab] 厳しい

40
00:04:26,451 --> 00:04:35,211
[Host] It means strict, harsh, or tough. Here it describes a hard, demanding situation — a hard time for the family budget.

41
00:04:35,812 --> 00:04:44,211
[Slow] お店では、少しでも安い肉を選ぶお客さんが増えているそうです。

42
00:04:45,012 --> 00:04:50,052
[Host] At the shops, it's said more customers are choosing even slightly cheaper meat.

43
00:04:50,651 --> 00:04:52,788
[Vocab] 選ぶ

44
00:04:53,187 --> 00:04:59,740
[Host] It means to choose, to pick. When prices rise, shoppers carefully choose the cheaper option.

45
00:05:00,339 --> 00:05:03,339
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
00:05:03,939 --> 00:05:06,699
[News] 今日のニュースです。

47
00:05:07,399 --> 00:05:13,184
[News] 鶏肉の値段が、今までで一番高くなりました。

48
00:05:13,884 --> 00:05:22,860
[News] 国の調査によると、鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、157円でした。

49
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:31,384
[News] これは、2015年に記録をとり始めてから、一番高い値段です。

50
00:05:32,084 --> 00:05:37,315
[News] 値段が上がった理由の一つは、円安です。

51
00:05:38,016 --> 00:05:44,783
[News] 円が安いと、外国から買うニワトリのエサが高くなります。

52
00:05:45,483 --> 00:05:52,827
[News] エサが高くなると、鶏肉を作るお金も増えて、値段が上がります。

53
00:05:53,528 --> 00:06:00,800
[News] 牛肉や、外国から運ばれる肉の値段も、高くなっています。

54
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:08,867
[News] 毎日の食事を作る家庭にとって、厳しい状況が続いています。

55
00:06:09,567 --> 00:06:16,911
[News] お店では、少しでも安い肉を選ぶお客さんが増えているそうです。

56
00:06:17,612 --> 00:06:20,348
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

57
00:06:20,947 --> 00:06:27,860
[Slow] 鶏肉の値段は、今までと比べてどうなりましたか。

58
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:33,411
[Host] How does the price of chicken compare to before? It became the highest ever.

59
00:06:34,012 --> 00:06:40,875
[Slow] 鶏肉100グラムの平均の値段は、いくらでしたか。

60
00:06:41,675 --> 00:06:47,531
[Host] What was the average price of one hundred grams of chicken? One hundred fifty-seven yen.

61
00:06:48,132 --> 00:06:53,795
[Slow] 値段が上がった理由の一つは、何ですか。

62
00:06:54,596 --> 00:06:58,076
[Host] What is one reason the price went up? The weak yen.

63
00:06:58,675 --> 00:07:11,060
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

64
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:13,915
[News] また明日。
